  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.45 Insecticide",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.45 “Insecticide” means a pesticide product that is designed for use against insects or other arthropods, but excluding products that are:\n\n(a) For agricultural use;\n\n(b) For a use that requires a structural pest control license under New Hampshire law; or\n\n(c) Restricted materials that require a permit for use and possession.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24 (formerly Env-A 4103.46)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
